00:14:52.000 --> 00:15:55.000
Brad and the detectives drove to the residence where Brad signed a form consenting to a search of the property. He waited outside while one detective entered to look for Tammy and the other went to search her vehicle. Upon entering the garage, the detectives saw a reddish-brown stain on the door of Tammy's Durango. This is what he'd noticed earlier when looking through the window and had suspected it was blood. As he moved closer, he also saw what appeared to be blood dripping from the vehicle's side running board. Each drop fell in a small pool on the concrete floor below at a rate that indicated someone had lost a significant amount of blood. The detective opened the Durango's back door and was overwhelmed by the strong stench of bleach. He noticed swirls on the vehicle's upholstery that suggested someone had tried to wipe something up.
布拉德和侦探们开车来到住所，布拉德在表单上签字同意对房产进行搜查。他在外面等候，而一名侦探进去寻找塔米，另一名去搜查她的车。一进入车库，侦探就看到塔米杜兰戈车门上有红褐色的污渍。这就是他之前透过窗户看时注意到并怀疑是血迹的东西。当他走近时，他还看到似乎有血迹从车辆的侧踏板上滴落下来。每一滴都落在了下方混凝土地面上的一个小血泊中，其速度表明有人流了大量的血。侦探打开杜兰戈的后门，被强烈的漂白剂气味熏得喘不过气来。他注意到车内装饰上有漩涡状的擦痕，这表明有人曾试图擦拭掉什么。

19
00:15:55.000 --> 00:17:01.000
Everything about the situation suggested foul play, but the detective didn't want to alert Brad to what he'd found. Brad could withdraw his consent for the search at any time, and the detective wanted to secure an official search warrant before the homeowner changed his mind. Instead, the two detectives asked Brad to join them at the station to answer some questions. While he was away from home, they would covertly apply for a search warrant. Meanwhile, Haley was sitting in class worrying about her mother when a message suddenly blared over the loudspeaker summoning her to the front office. Haley's mind started to race. She nervously walked to the office and was greeted by a police officer who wanted to ask her some questions about her parents' relationship. Haley said that her mom and dad didn't fight and there had never been any violence between them.
情况的一切都表明发生了谋杀犯罪，但侦探不想惊动布拉德让他知道自己发现了什么。布拉德随时可以撤回对搜查的同意，侦探希望在房主改变主意之前获得一份正式的搜查令。相反，这两名侦探要求布拉德和他们一起去警局回答一些问题。在他离开家期间，他们将秘密申请搜查令。与此同时，海莉坐在教室里为母亲担心，这时扩音器里突然传出一个声音，命令她去前台办公室。海莉的心思开始飞转。她紧张地走向办公室，迎面走来一名警察，想问她一些关于父母关系的问题。海莉说她的爸爸妈妈不吵架，他们之间从来没有过任何暴力。

20
00:17:01.000 --> 00:18:10.000
Because of this, the recent news of their divorce had been very unexpected. When she had gone to bed the night before, Tammy was at home and nothing seemed out of the ordinary. While Haley was being questioned, police contacted some of Tammy's friends and family to see if they knew where Tammy could be. There was a reason why Tammy's mother hadn't contacted Brad when Tammy missed their early morning phone call. During the recent Christmas break, Tammy had visited her family in Wyoming and told them she planned on leaving her husband. Tammy's family suspected she might have been seeing someone else as she had mentioned Brian's name several times, but they had impressed her on the matter. Brad had even called Tammy's mother Bonnie asking for her help to save their marriage, but it was clear that Tammy had already made up her mind. Back at the peer police station, Brad was cooperative as detectives sat him down for a chat.
正因为如此，最近传出他们离婚的消息非常出乎意料。前一天晚上她睡觉时，塔米在家，一切看起来都很正常。在对海莉进行盘问的同时，警方联系了塔米的一些朋友和家人，看他们是否知道塔米会在哪里。塔米没有在清晨错过电话时联系布拉德是有原因的。在最近的圣诞假期期间，塔米曾去怀俄明州探望家人，并告诉他们她计划离开丈夫。塔米的家人怀疑她可能在和别人交往，因为她多次提到布莱恩的名字，但他们没有在这个问题上逼问她。布拉德甚至给塔米的母亲邦妮打电话寻求她的帮助以挽救他们的婚姻，但很明显塔米已经下定决心了。回到皮尔警察局，当侦探们让布拉德坐下来谈话时，他非常配合。

21
00:18:10.000 --> 00:19:09.000
He told them that Tammy had recently revealed she was dating another man and wanted a divorce, but Brad didn't know who the other man was or where he lived. He said that he didn't want to know and wasn't curious to find out. Brad strongly denied having anything to do with Tammy's disappearance and insisted he had no idea where she could be. When the detectives told Brad that blood had been found on the running board of Tammy's Durango, he was visibly shocked. He admitted he was the last person to drive the vehicle when attempting to trail Tammy the night before, repeating his story about breaking down and a highway patrol officer offering assistance. Brad insisted that after restarting the car, he drove straight home. He didn't recall hitting an animal or anything else.
他告诉他们，塔米最近透露她正在和另一个男人约会并想要离婚，但布拉德不知道另一个男人是谁，也不知道他住在哪里。他说他不想知道，也没有好奇去查明。布拉德强烈否认自己与塔米的失踪有任何关系，并坚信自己不知道她会在哪里。当侦探们告诉布拉德在塔米的杜兰戈车的踏板上发现了血迹时，他明显感到震惊。他承认自己在前一天晚上试图尾随塔米时是最后一个驾驶该车的人，并重复了他关于车子抛锚以及公路巡警提供协助的说法。布拉德坚信重新启动汽车后，他直接开车回了家。他不记得撞过动物或其他任何东西。

22
00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:58.000
When he got home, he parked the Durango in the garage. If Tammy or anyone else had returned to retrieve the vehicle, he didn't know about it. While Brad was questioned, the search warrant for his house was approved. Police examined each room, but nothing appeared to be out of place. The beds were all made and the washer and dryer were filled with clean laundry. There was no sign of Tammy and no indication that anything untoward had happened. Other than the blood in Tammy's vehicle, it appeared to be a warm and loving family home. Yet, when investigators swabbed the Durango for forensic evidence,
他回到家时，把杜兰戈车停在了车库里。如果塔米或其他任何人回来取过车，他并不知道。在对布拉德进行盘问的同时，对他家的搜查令也获批了。警方检查了每一个房间，但没有发现任何异常。床都铺好了，洗衣机和烘干机里装满了干净的衣物。没有塔米的踪迹，也没有任何迹象表明发生过什么不寻常的事情。除了塔米车上的血迹之外，这看起来像是一个温馨而充满爱的家庭。然而，当调查人员用棉签擦拭杜兰戈以获取法医证据时，

23
00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:47.000
they realized that there was much more blood than they initially thought. Samples were sent to a forensic lab along with some of Tammy's personal belongings to confirm whether it was a match for her DNA. The interviewing detectives were at a loss. Brad didn't have a criminal record and there was no evidence to suggest he was responsible for Tammy's disappearance. However, the amount of blood found in her car indicated she had been seriously harmed and most likely killed. If this was the case, Brad was the most likely suspect. He had access to Tammy's car and her desire for a divorce suggested an obvious motive.
他们意识到血迹比他们最初想象的要多得多。样本被送到法医实验室，连同塔米的一些个人物品一起，以确认是否与她的DNA相匹配。负责问话的侦探们一筹莫展。布拉德没有犯罪前科，也没有证据表明他对塔米的失踪负有责任。然而，在她车里发现的血迹量表明她受到了严重的伤害，并且极有可能是被杀害了。如果是这样的话，布拉德是最有可能的嫌疑人。他有接触塔米汽车的途径，而她想要离婚则提供了一个明显的动机。

24
00:20:47.000 --> 00:21:43.000
The problem was, without a body, they couldn't even be certain that Tammy was dead. Brad was interrogated for five hours, with detectives slowly increasing the pressure. Despite their persistent questioning, Brad continued to deny having any knowledge of Tammy's whereabouts. Desperate for answers, the detectives flatly accused him of lying. This accusation was the final straw for Brad. He asked for a lawyer. Now, the detectives were faced with a difficult decision. They still couldn't be 100% certain that Tammy was dead, but all signs pointed to homicide. If Brad was responsible and they let him go, it would give him an opportunity to destroy any potential evidence.
问题在于，没有尸体，他们甚至无法确定塔米已经死了。布拉德被审讯了五个小时，侦探们的压力步步升级。尽管他们坚持不懈地盘问，布拉德仍然否认自己知道塔米的下落。迫切想要答案的侦探们直截了当地指责他在撒谎。这个指责成了压垮布拉德的最后一根稻草。他要求请律师。现在，侦探们面临着一个艰难的决定。他们仍然无法百分之百确定塔米已经死了，但所有的迹象都指向谋杀。如果布拉德是罪魁祸首而他们放了他，这会给他销毁任何潜在证据的机会。

25
00:21:43.000 --> 00:22:48.000
Under pressure to make a call, they abruptly arrested Brad for first-degree murder, setting bail at $100,000. Brad was incredulous and staunchly maintained his innocence. Haley was placed in foster care overnight as Tammy's family in Wyoming were brought up to speed with what was going on. Unable to bear the thought of Haley being on her own, Tammy's father got in his car and began the nearly nine-hour drive to be with his granddaughter. Brad's friends were stunned to learn he'd been arrested for murder. Brad was a gentle family man, and they couldn't imagine him ever raising a hand to his wife, let alone launching a vicious and deadly attack. However, they weren't surprised to hear that he hadn't pushed Tammy for information about the other man she was seeing. Brad was a mild-mannered person, hounding Tammy wouldn't be in his nature.
在做出决定的压力下，他们突然以一级谋杀罪逮捕了布拉德，保释金定为10万美元。布拉德难以置信，坚决坚称自己是无辜的。海莉连夜被送入寄养家庭，而塔米在怀俄明州的家人则被告知了所发生的事情。无法忍受海莉独自一人呆着的想法，塔米的父亲上了车，开始了近九个小时的驾车行程去陪伴他的外孙女。布拉德的朋友们得知他因谋杀被捕时都惊呆了。布拉德是一个温和顾家的好男人，他们无法想象他会对妻子动一根手指，更不用说发动残酷致命的攻击了。然而，听到他没有向塔米追问她所交往的另一个男人的信息，他们并不感到惊讶。布拉德是一个温和的人，纠缠塔米不是他的天性。

26
00:22:48.000 --> 00:23:47.000
With Brad in custody, the next step for detectives was to question Tammy's boyfriend, Brian Clark. He was summoned to the police station and arrived with a lawyer by his side. Like Tammy, Brian was also married with a daughter. The two co-workers had initially hit it off as friends, but their friendship had slowly become physical and blossomed into a romance. Brian told detectives the last time he saw Tammy was on the afternoon of Tuesday, February 7, the day before she went missing. The two had met at the Fawn Motel in Peer. Afterwards, Brian dropped Tammy home at around 5pm. From there, he attended a local basketball game with his wife and daughter.
随着布拉德被拘留，侦探们的下一步是审问塔米的男友布莱恩·克拉克。他被传唤到警察局，在律师的陪同下到达。和塔米一样，布莱恩也已结婚并育有一个女儿。这两个同事最初作为朋友一拍即合，但他们的友谊慢慢发展成肉体关系并绽放为浪漫恋情。布莱恩告诉侦探，他最后一次见到塔米是在2月7日星期二下午，也就是她失踪前一天。两人在皮尔的法恩汽车旅馆（Fawn Motel）见了面。之后，布莱恩在大约下午5点把塔米送回家。从那里，他和妻子女儿一起去观看当地的一场篮球比赛。

27
00:23:47.000 --> 00:24:44.000
When the game finished, he went home with his family and didn't leave the house again until going to work the next morning. Brian said his wife could verify his alibi. The only problem was that she didn't know about his affair with Tammy and he didn't want her to know. He was reluctant for police to question her as there would be no way to do so without revealing this information. Once again, the detectives weren't sure what to think. Brian seemed genuine, but the fact that he'd already retained and brought a lawyer with him seemed suspicious. If he was innocent, why did he feel compelled to seek legal counsel from the get-go? The fact that Brian's wife didn't know about his affair with Tammy also gave Brian a strong motive for murder.
比赛结束后，他和家人一起回家，直到第二天早上上班才再次出门。布赖恩说他的妻子可以为他的不在场证明作证。唯一的问题是，她并不知道他和塔米有染，而他也不想让她知道。他不愿让警察盘问她，因为这样做势必会暴露这一秘密。侦探们再次陷入了迷茫，不知该作何感想。布赖恩看起来很真诚，但他已经请了律师并将其带在身边的这一事实却显得十分可疑。如果他是清白的，为什么从一开始就觉得有必要寻求法律顾问呢？布赖恩的妻子对他和塔米的私情一无所知这一事实，也让布赖恩多了一个重大的谋杀动机。

28
00:24:44.000 --> 00:25:51.000
Perhaps after Tammy came clean to Brad about her relationship with Brian, she had pushed Brian to do the same with his spouse. Maybe she wanted Brian to get a divorce, but he wasn't prepared to do so. Tammy might have threatened to approach Brian's wife herself, which could have pushed him over the edge. The blood pointed towards Brad, who undisputedly had access to Tammy's vehicle. However, if Brad was telling the truth about trailing Tammy and her boyfriend in the early morning hours of Wednesday, February 8, it was possible that Brian had killed Tammy and then planted blood on her vehicle in an attempt to frame Brad. Both men had a motive, but only one of them could be telling the truth. Inquiries were made with the Highway Patrol Unit to check Brad's claim that he'd broken down while trailing Tammy.
比赛结束后，他和家人一起回家，再也没有离开过家，直到第二天早上上班。布拉德向公路巡查队进行了查询，以核实他尾随塔米时汽车抛锚的说法。

29
00:25:51.000 --> 00:26:57.000
Dashcam footage confirmed that at 1.40am, a state trooper had found the derango pulled over on the side of the road with Brad rear behind the wheel. The trooper asked Brad for ID, but he said he didn't have any as he was just ducking out to grab something from the store. He willingly provided his full name, and the trooper didn't notice anything suspicious about his behaviour. Nor did he see anything strange in or on the car. Once Brad got the car started again, he drove off in the direction of his home. The detectives now had confirmation of the story he had consistently told them from the beginning. With so many unanswered questions, the case couldn't progress any further until Tammy was found. When morning broke on Thursday, February 9, a search party made up of police officers, firefighters and local volunteers
行车记录仪画面证实，凌晨1点40分，一名州警发现那辆杜兰戈车停在路边，布拉德坐在驾驶座后面。警察向布拉德索要身份证，但他说自己没有带，因为他只是出来从商店买点东西。他爽快地报出了自己的全名，警察没有发现他有任何可疑的行为。也没有在车内或车上发现任何奇怪的地方。布拉德重新发动汽车后，朝他家的方向开去。侦探们现在证实了他从一开始就一直讲述的故事。由于有这么多未解之谜，在找到塔米之前，案件无法取得进一步进展。2月9日星期四破晓时分，由警察、消防员和当地志愿者组成的搜寻队

30
00:26:57.000 --> 00:28:00.000
gathered to comb the vast countryside surrounding Peer. Time was of the essence. The hills around the city saw very little foot traffic, except for the hunters who flocked to the area between October and January. Hunting season had just concluded. This meant that if Tammy was lying undiscovered in the area, it was highly unlikely that anyone would come across her body until the next hunting season began in eight months time. By that point, wild animals would have likely found her first. On foot and with the help of cadaver dogs, the search party covered mile upon mile of the rolling hills and prairies. Law enforcement managed to secure a helicopter from the National Guard to cover the area overhead, but even with the advantage of a bird's eye view, there was no sign of Tammy anywhere.
聚集在一起，对皮尔周边广袤的乡村进行了地毯式搜寻。时间就是生命。这座城市周围的山丘极少有人涉足，除了10月到1月蜂拥至该地区的猎人们。狩猎季刚刚结束。这意味着如果塔米不为人知地躺在这个地区，在8个月后下一个狩猎季开始之前，极不可能有人会偶然发现她的尸体。到那个时候，野生动物可能已经先找到她了。搜寻队靠步行并在搜尸犬的协助下，搜寻了起伏的山丘和草原一英里又一英里。执法部门设法从国民警卫队调来了一架直升机从空中搜寻该地区，但即使有鸟瞰视角的优势，到处也看不到塔米的踪迹。

31
00:28:00.000 --> 00:29:04.000
As the sun began to descend for the day, the helicopter pilot decided to do one last sweep of an isolated prairie approximately 10 miles north of Peer. As they passed over a spillway running off the Awahi dam, they noticed something in the rugged terrain below. It was the naked body of Tammy Rhea. Tammy had been stabbed upwards of 35 times and her throat had been slashed. It appeared that some of the injuries had been made after she was already dead, sometime after the initial attack. Her hands were covered in knife wounds, indicating she had attempted to fight off her killer. One cut was so deep that the bone had been exposed, as though Tammy had taken hold of the knife during the attack. It was the most extreme case of overkill that attending detectives had ever witnessed.
当太阳开始西沉时，直升机飞行员决定对皮尔以北大约10英里处的一个偏远草原进行最后一次巡视。当他们飞越奥瓦希大坝延伸出的泄洪道时，他们注意到下方崎岖的地形中有东西。那是塔米·里亚赤裸的尸体。塔米被刺了35刀以上，喉咙也被割断。看起来有些伤是在她已经死后才造成的，在最初的袭击发生一段时间之后。她的双手布满刀伤，表明她曾试图击退凶手。其中一处伤口非常深，连骨头都露出来了，就像塔米在袭击过程中抓住过刀子一样。这是在场侦探们见过的最极端残忍的过度杀戮案件。

32
00:29:04.000 --> 00:30:08.000
Yet, there was no blood on the scene, meaning that the attack itself had occurred elsewhere. Officers searched the area for clues and found a t-shirt shredded with knife cuts, as well as a pair of blood-stained gloves. Nothing was found that identified the killer. Tammy's father, Don, was nearing Peer on his drive from Wyoming when his cell phone rang and a police officer broke the dreaded news that Tammy's body had been found. To save him the pain of seeing her injuries, Don was told he wouldn't need to formally identify his daughter. Haley had been hoping with all her might that her mother would be found alive. When she received the terrible news, she refused to believe that Brad could be responsible. There was no way that the father she knew could be capable of such a heinous crime.
然而，现场没有血迹，这意味着袭击本身发生在其他地方。警察在现场搜寻线索，找到了一件被刀割破的T恤以及一双沾满血迹的手套。没有发现任何可以确认凶手身份的物品。塔米的父亲唐（Don）从怀俄明州驾车正接近皮尔时，手机响了，一名警官打破了令人恐惧的消息：塔米的尸体被找到了。为了免除他看到女儿伤势的痛苦，唐被告知他不需要正式辨认女儿的尸体。海莉曾竭尽全力希望母亲能活着被找到。当她听到这个可怕的消息时，她拒绝相信布拉德会是罪魁祸首。她认识的父亲绝不可能做出如此凶残的罪行。

33
00:30:08.000 --> 00:31:07.000
Tammy's body was autopsyed, but it didn't reveal any forensic evidence tying either Brad or Brian to her murder. Police returned to the Rhea property and conducted another search, this time testing surfaces around the house with luminal. Once again, they found nothing. Tammy and Brad had been sleeping in separate bedrooms and both their beds were microscopically examined, but there was no trace of blood anywhere. Investigators began to wonder if they had arrested an innocent man. The evidence simply wasn't adding up against Brad Rhea. Instead, they turned their attention to Brian Clark. They had no choice but to question Brian's wife, Kerry, not her real name, in turn forcing Brian to break the news to her about his affair with Tammy.
塔米的尸体被进行了尸检，但没有发现任何将布拉德或布莱恩与她的谋杀案联系起来的法医证据。警察返回里亚的住所进行了另一次搜查，这次用鲁米诺（luminol）试剂测试了房子周围的表面。他们再次一无所获。塔米和布拉德一直睡在不同的卧室里，他们的床都经过了显微镜级别的检查，但到处都没有血迹的痕迹。调查人员开始怀疑他们是否逮捕了一个无辜的人。证据根本无法指证布拉德·里亚。相反，他们将注意力转向了布莱恩·克拉克。他们别无选择，只能盘问布莱恩的妻子克里（Kerry，化名），这反过来迫使布莱恩向她坦白了他与塔米的外遇。

34
00:31:07.000 --> 00:32:07.000
Kerry was obviously crushed, but when the detectives asked her about Brian's whereabouts on the night of Tuesday, February 7, she confirmed that he had been with her and their daughter at a local basketball game. Afterwards, they spent the rest of the night at home. But there was one problem. Although Kerry and Brian shared at the same bedroom, Kerry suffered from ongoing back pain and sometimes slept in a recliner chair downstairs. The night Tammy was killed, she had slept in the recliner. This meant it was possible that Brian had sneaked out in the middle of the night without his wife's knowledge. Brad remained in custody while the investigation continued. Haley hoped the police would find the evidence to clear her father so that she wouldn't have to live without both of her parents.
