50
00:46:17.000 --> 00:47:32.000
Brad had been driving in the direction of Brian Clark's house, and it was possible that he had been heading there with the intention of planting evidence. He'd likely assumed the condom would be found and DNA testing would link it back to Brian, thereby framing him for the murder. But, once Brad realized this key piece of evidence was missed during Tammies autopsy, he hatched a scheme to write false confession letters and enlisted his twin brother's help to send them from outside of jail. At the time of Brad's arrest, traces of vegetation were found on his shoes. These were tested and confirmed to match the Juniper bushes where the blood-soaked evidence was dumped. Furthermore, the garbage bags used to dispose of the evidence were the exact same kind as others found inside the Rhea home. This is undisputedly placed here at the crime scene, and the existence of the tarp indicated premeditation. With all of these elements combined, the prosecution finally felt they had a strong enough case to take Brad to trial.
布拉德当时正朝布赖恩·克拉克的房子方向开车，有可能他当时正打算去那里栽赃证据。他很可能以为避孕套会被发现，而DNA检测会将其与布赖恩联系起来，从而将谋杀罪嫁祸给他。但是，一旦布拉德意识到这一关键证据在塔米的尸检中被漏掉了，他便策划了虚假供词信件，并拉拢他的双胞胎兄弟帮忙从监狱外面寄出。在布拉德被捕时，他的鞋上发现了植物残留物。经测试，这些残留物与倾倒血迹证据的杜松灌木完全吻合。此外，用于处理证据的垃圾袋与在雷亚家中发现的其他垃圾袋完全是同一类型。这无可争辩地将他与案发现场联系在一起，而防水布的存在则表明这是预谋作案。结合所有这些要素，检方终于觉得他们有足够的证据将布拉德送上法庭审判。

51
00:47:32.000 --> 00:48:40.000
The trial commenced in January of 2007, with Brad Rhea pleading not guilty to first-degree murder. Considering the death penalty wasn't being sought, South Dakota law dictated that if Brad was convicted, he'd automatically receive a mandatory life sentence. The prosecution anticipated a short trial for what they believed to be an open and shut case, but Brad made a rare decision for a defendant. He agreed to take the stand in his own defense. No one quite knew what to expect when it came time for him to testify. What he said shocked the courtroom, especially members of Tammy's family. Unable to conceal the lies any longer, Brad felt he finally had to come clean. It wasn't him who killed Tammy, but he's now 13-year-old daughter Haley.
审判于2007年1月开始，布拉德·雷亚对一级谋杀指控做出了无罪抗辩。考虑到检方并未寻求死刑，南达科他州法律规定，如果布拉德被定罪，他将自动面临强制性的终身监禁。检方原本预计这场看似板上钉钉的案件审理过程会很短，但布拉德做出了被告中罕见的决定。他同意出庭为自己作证。当轮到他作证时，没有人知道会发生什么。他在法庭上的言论震惊了所有人，尤其是塔米的家人。由于无法再掩盖谎言，布拉德觉得自己终于必须说出真相了。杀害塔米的不是他，而是他当时13岁的女儿海莉。

52
00:48:40.000 --> 00:49:34.000
He testified that the trouble began when he and Tammy told Haley they were getting a divorce. Haley was devastated. She liked her house and her family and didn't want anything to change. She was furious that her parents didn't want to work things out and had been depressed about the impending divorce for days. On the night of Tuesday, February 7, Brad came home late from work to find both Tammy and Haley already asleep. He went to bed himself, only to be awoken around midnight by the family's cat. He heard some noise from Tammy's room and went to see what it was. To his shock, he saw Haley standing over Tammy's body. She was covered in blood and holding a knife.
他作证说，麻烦始于他和塔米告诉海莉他们要离婚的时候。海莉心碎了。她喜欢她的房子和家庭，不希望任何事情改变。她对父母不愿修复关系感到愤怒，并且对即将到来的离婚情绪低落了好几天。2月7日星期二晚上，布拉德工作很晚回家，发现塔米和海莉都睡着了。他自己也上床睡觉了，但在午夜左右被家里的猫吵醒。他听到塔米房间里有动静，便过去查看是怎么回事。令他震惊的是，他看到海莉站在塔米的尸体上方。她浑身是血，手里拿着一把刀。

53
00:49:34.000 --> 00:50:16.000
Her nose was also bleeding as a result of being hit by Tammy as she fought back. Brad cried out, asking Haley what she'd done, but Haley didn't respond. She was catatonic. Brad jumped on Tammy and tried to give her mouth-to-mouth resuscitation, but it was no use. She was already dead. Haley showed no emotion or reaction and seemed barely conscious. It was then that Brad realized she was sleepwalking. In a panic, he carried Haley back to bed and wiped all the blood off of her.
由于遭到拼命反抗的塔米殴打，她的鼻子也在流血。布拉德大声质问海莉做了什么，但海莉没有回应。她处于紧张性精神症（木僵）状态。布拉德扑向塔米，试图给她做人工呼吸，但无济于事。她已经死了。海莉没有表现出任何情绪或反应，几乎毫无意识。就在那时，布拉德意识到她在梦游。在惊慌失措中，他把海莉抱回床上，擦掉了她身上的血迹。

54
00:50:16.000 --> 00:51:28.000
Then he tried to clean up the crime scene. He bundled up the blood-soaked bed linens, threw their bloodied clothing in the washing machine, and carried Tammy's body into her car. Wanting to protect his daughter, he made the snap decision to plant the condom in an attempt to blame the man Tammy was dating. When Haley woke the next day, she acted completely normal, and it was clear to Brad that she had no recollection of what had happened. His initial plan had been to take Haley and flee to Mexico, but he was arrested before he could act on it. Brad said Haley had always exhibited some troubling behaviors, claiming that when she was a child, she used to stab her stuffed animals. Brad knew his daughter needed psychological treatment, but didn't think she'd get it if she was sent to prison, so he decided to lie to authorities to protect her. He acknowledged that he'd broken the law and should be charged accordingly.
然后他试图清理案发现场。他把沾满血迹的床单卷起来，把他们带血的衣服扔进洗衣机，并把塔米的尸体搬进她的车里。出于保护女儿的愿望，他临时做出决定，将避孕套放进体内，企图将罪名推给塔米正在约会的那个男人。海莉第二天醒来时，表现得完全正常，布拉德清楚她对发生的事情毫无记忆。他最初的计划是带着海莉逃往墨西哥，但他在付诸行动之前就被捕了。布拉德说海莉一直表现出一些令人不安的行为，并声称她小时候曾刺伤过她的毛绒玩具。布拉德知道女儿需要心理治疗，但认为如果她被送进监狱就无法接受治疗，于是他决定向当局撒谎来保护她。他承认自己触犯了法律，应该受到相应的指控。

55
00:51:28.000 --> 00:52:56.000
But because his lies were based on the desire to protect his daughter, he urged the jury not to find him guilty of murder. Brad's lawyer argued that because Haley was unconscious when she stabbed Tammy, she couldn't be held legally responsible, telling the jury, there's a lot that could have been going on between Haley and Tammy without us knowing about it. He referenced Haley's strong athletic abilities, with particular focus on her volleyball skills, indicating that her overarm serving style was similar to the downward stabbing motion used in Tammy's murder. The defense lawyer said, if Brad Rhea is telling us the truth, shame on us all. Brad watched intently as Haley was put on the stand. She vehemently denied his accusations. Haley spoke of her deep love for her mother and said she would never have done anything to hurt her. This contrasted with her relationship to her father. Haley had never been very close to Brad and was now afraid of him. On the night of Tammy's murder, Haley went to sleep with her bedroom door open.
但由于他的谎言是基于保护女儿的愿望，他敦促陪审团不要判处他谋杀罪。布拉德的律师辩称，由于海莉刺伤塔米时处于无意识状态，因此她不应承担法律责任，他告诉陪审团：“海莉和塔米之间可能发生了很多我们不知道的事情。”他提到了海莉强劲的运动能力，特别是专注于她的排球技能，暗示她的上臂发球风格类似于塔米谋杀案中使用的向下刺击动作。辩护律师说：“如果布拉德·雷亚对我们说的是实话，那我们所有人都该感到羞耻。”海莉出庭时，布拉德目不转睛地看着她。她强烈否认了他的指控。海莉谈到了她对母亲的深切爱意，并表示她绝不会做任何伤害母亲的事。这与她和父亲的关系形成了鲜明对比。海莉从未与布拉德很亲近，现在甚至有些害怕他。在塔米遇害的那天晚上，海莉睡觉时卧室的门是开着的。

56
00:52:56.000 --> 00:54:01.000
At around midnight, she woke up to find it was closed. Her father opened the door and was holding an armful of clothing. Haley asked what he was doing, to which Brad replied, nothing. He put the clothes down and laid down in Haley's bed, telling her he loved her. Haley fell back asleep and when she woke the next morning, her mother was gone and her father was doing laundry. When she had asked him where her mother was, Brad had initially claimed she was in her room. But Haley had checked the entire house and there was no trace of Tammy. As for the lawyer's inference that she was capable of stabbing her mother based on her volleyball serve, Haley said she didn't use an overarm serve at all, but an underarm one. The prosecution was outraged by Brad's claim that Haley was the killer.
大约在午夜时分，她醒来发现门被关上了。她的父亲打开门，手里抱着一大堆衣服。海莉问他在做什么，布拉德回答说：“没什么。”他放下衣服，躺在海莉的床上，告诉她他爱她。海莉又睡着了，第二天早上醒来时，她的母亲不见了，父亲正在洗衣服。当她问他母亲在哪里时，布拉德最初声称她在自己的房间里。但海莉检查了整个房子，根本没有塔米的踪迹。至于律师根据她的排球发球推断她有能力刺死母亲的说法，海莉说她根本不使用上臂发球，而是用下臂发球。检方对布拉德声称海莉是凶手的说法感到愤怒。

57
00:54:01.000 --> 00:55:20.000
The stab wounds on Tammy's body were incredibly deep, some two inches longer than the blade of the weapon itself. The sheer force of the knife wounds alone couldn't have been afflicted by someone of Haley's size, nor did she have any history of sleepwalking. During cross-examination, Brad said that he and Tammy had a happy marriage, but his long work hours had ultimately driven her away. Arguing against Haley's claim that she wasn't close with him, Brad claimed they were so close that he was willing to go to prison for her. Brad's testimony only served to hurt his defense, as he gave inconsistent answers to facts that had already been established. He claimed he didn't know Tammy was having an affair until after he was arrested, even though he'd already admitted this fact to detectives when Tammy was first reported missing. He also claimed that the blood Haley was covered in was predominantly from her bloody nose, not Tammy's injuries. Given how many wounds were inflicted, this seemed highly unlikely.
塔米身上的刀伤极其深，有些比凶器本身的刀刃还要长两英寸。仅凭刀伤的纯粹力量，是不可能由海莉这样身材的人造成的，而且她也没有任何梦游史。在盘问过程中，布拉德声称他和塔米婚姻美满，但自己长时间的工作最终逼走了她。针对海莉“与他并不亲密”的说法，布拉德辩称他们关系非常亲密，以至于他愿意为她入狱。布拉德的证词只会削弱他的辩护，因为他对已经确立的事实给出了矛盾的回答。他声称直到被捕后才知道塔米有婚外情，尽管在塔米最初被报失踪时，他已经向侦探承认了这一事实。他还声称海莉身上沾满的血主要是她自己流鼻血的血，而不是塔米受伤的血。考虑到造成的伤口数量，这显得极不可信。

58
00:55:20.000 --> 00:56:24.000
Similarly, he said that when giving Tammy mouth-to-mouth resuscitation, he didn't notice any stab wounds, just blood. Given the amount of injuries to Tammy's chest, the prosecution argued it would have been impossible not to notice the wounds if Brad really did attempt to revive her. Brad's attempt to place the blame on his daughter was fruitless. His brother, Brett, had already admitted to writing the letters aimed at framing Brian Clark. After his arrest, Brett had cooperated fully with investigators, agreeing to testify against his twin in exchange for being released from jail after serving 172 days. Brett said he was genuinely sorry for the part he played and regretted trying to help Brad. Brett told the court his brother deserved to be sent to prison. He was released immediately after testifying.
同样，他说在给塔米做人工呼吸时，他没有注意到任何刀伤，只有血。鉴于塔米胸部的伤势数量，检方辩称，如果布拉德真的试图对她进行复活急救，绝不可能注意不到这些伤口。布拉德试图将罪责推卸给女儿的企图毫无结果。他的兄弟布雷特已经承认写了旨在陷害布赖恩·克拉克的信件。被捕后，布雷特全力配合调查人员，同意指证他的双胞胎兄弟，以此换取在服刑172天后被释放出狱。布雷特表示，他对自己所扮演的角色感到真诚的抱歉，并后悔曾试图帮助布拉德。布雷特告诉法庭，他的兄弟罪有应得，应该被送进监狱。他在作证后立即被释放。

59
00:56:24.000 --> 00:57:15.000
The judge believed he had already suffered enough. The twins' mother had recently passed away from an aneurysm after visiting her sons in jail. It was also revealed just how Brad had figured out who Tammy was dating. He'd bugged her car with the audio recording device and then placed a bunch of flowers in the vehicle along with a letter that read, I'm sorry, let's make up. Just as Brad had hoped, Tammy thought the flowers were from her boyfriend and called Brian to thank him, thus revealing his identity to Brad. It took the jury just three hours to find Brad Rhea guilty of first-degree murder.
法官认为他已经受够了折磨。这对双胞胎的母亲在探望完在监狱里的儿子们后不久，便因动脉瘤不幸离世。调查人员还揭露了布拉德是如何弄清楚塔米在和谁约会的。他在她的车里安装了录音设备，然后在车里放了一束花以及一封信，上面写着：“对不起，我们和好吧。”正如布拉德所希望的那样，塔米以为这些花是男友送的，便打电话给布赖恩向他致谢，从而将他的身份暴露给了布拉德。陪审团仅用了三个小时就裁定布拉德·雷亚一级谋杀罪名成立。

60
00:57:15.000 --> 00:57:57.000
His attempt to place the blame on Hailey had made him look more guilty and only served to anger members of the jury. The prosecutor stated, Brad was one of the best witnesses I had. His testimony hurt him a bunch. Following the verdict, Tammy's family released a statement that read, Justice was finally served and all the lies can stop. Tammy was such a wonderful person with such a zest for life. Unfortunately, she was not given an opportunity to make a better life for herself and Hailey.
他试图将责任推给海莉的举动让他看起来更加罪责难逃，并只招致了陪审团成员的愤怒。检察官表示：“布拉德是我遇到的最好的证人之一。他的证词对他的伤害极大。”裁决宣布后，塔米的家人发表了一份声明，上面写道：“正义终于得以伸张，所有的谎言都可以停止了。塔米是一个如此美好、对生活充满热情的人。不幸的是，她没有机会为自己和海莉创造更好的生活。”

61
00:57:57.000 --> 00:58:41.000
Despite the mandatory life sentence for first-degree murder, an official sentencing date was set so that Tammy's loved ones could have their moment to speak about the impact the murder had on their lives. Hailey chose not to speak, instead providing the judge with an undisclosed written statement. As Tammy's mother Bonnie addressed the courtroom, Brad Rhea stood with his eyes glued to the floor. Bonnie said, We trusted you for so many years and you deceived us. You have taken all that you can from this family. On this earth, you will not receive enough punishment for your heinous crime.
尽管一级谋杀罪面临强制性的终身监禁，法庭还是正式设定了一个宣判日期，以便塔米的亲人们有机会就这起谋杀对他们生活的冲击发表感言。海莉选择不发言，而是向法官提交了一份未公开的书面声明。当塔米的母亲邦尼走向法庭发言时，布拉德·雷亚双眼死死盯着地板。邦尼说：“我们信任了你这么多年，你却欺骗了我们。你已经从这个家庭夺走了你所能夺走的一切。在这个大地上，你所受到的惩罚永远无法弥补你那残忍的罪行。”

62
00:58:41.000 --> 00:59:27.000
She added that Brad should be ashamed of himself for trying to blame his own daughter, quipping, I'm surprised you didn't try to blame the cat. A video slideshow celebrating Tammy's life was played, but Brad showed zero emotion. At no point did he apologize. He seemed intent on sticking to his story that Hailey was the real killer, telling the court, I gave up my life because I love her. The judge concluded that Brad was a calculated, cold-blooded murderer, motivated to kill Tammy out of revenge for her having an affair and wanting a divorce.
她补充说，布拉德试图将罪责推给自己的亲生女儿，这让他感到极其羞耻，并讽刺道：“我很惊讶你居然没有试图把罪名推给那只猫。”法庭播放了一个庆祝塔米一生的视频幻灯片，但布拉德毫无情绪波动。他自始至终没有道歉。他似乎铁了心要坚持“海莉才是真正的凶手”这一谎言，对法庭说：“我放弃了我的人生，因为我爱她。”法官总结指出，布拉德是一个蓄谋已久、冷血的凶手，杀害塔米的动机是为了报复她出轨并执意要离婚。

63
00:59:27.000 --> 01:00:14.000
She told Brad he had unsuccessfully attempted to paint himself as the victim. Quote, You are not a victim, you are a predator. Along with a life sentence, the judge ordered that Brad be forbidden from having contact with Hailey or Tammy's family ever again. Brad tried to appeal the conviction and called for a retrial. He argued that Hailey's DNA was never compared to DNA found at the crime scene, and that his defense lawyer had failed him by not pursuing any other DNA evidence. He also claimed that investigators had falsified evidence against him.
她告诉布拉德，他试图把自己粉饰成受害者的企图以失败告终。“引用：你不是受害者，你是一个掠夺者。”除了判处终身监禁外，法官还下令禁止布拉德再与海莉或塔米的家人有任何接触。布拉德试图对定罪提出上诉并要求重审。他辩称，海莉的DNA从未与案发现场的DNA进行过比对，并且他的辩护律师没有追求任何其他DNA证据，这辜负了他。他还声称调查人员伪造了对不利于他的证据。

64
01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:49.000
His appeal was unanimously rejected. Hailey Rhea lost both parents on the day her father made the decision to murder her mother. She went to live with Tammy's family in Wyoming and never saw Brad again. In the wake of the crime, Tammy's sister Holly told NBC reporter Josh Mankiewicz, Quote, The best you can do is try to stay strong forever. Quote, The best you can do is try to stay strong for Hailey.
他的上诉被一致驳回。海莉·雷亚在父亲做出谋杀母亲决定的那一天，失去了双亲。她搬去怀俄明州与塔米的家人同住，再也没有见过布拉德。在这场悲剧之后，塔米的姐姐霍利对全国广播公司（NBC）记者乔希·曼基维茨说：“引用：你能做的最好的事情，就是努力永远保持坚强。”“引用：你能做的最好的事情，就是为了海莉努力坚强下去。”

65
01:00:49.000 --> 01:01:29.000
It's really like having someone cut your arm off. I mean, it's a piece of you that you never get back. And thank goodness we still have Hailey, because she is so much like her mum. Tammy's family successfully filed a wrongful death lawsuit against Brad for $5.3 million, while Brad didn't have that much money. The ruling allowed them to sell off his personal property and give the proceeds to Hailey. Growing up without Tammy was incredibly difficult for Hailey, but she refused to let the tragedy define her.
这真的就像有人砍掉了你的一条胳膊。我的意思是，那是你永远无法找回的一部分自己。谢天谢地，我们身边还有海莉，因为她和她的妈妈太像了。”塔米的家人成功对布拉德提起了非法致死民事诉讼，索赔530万美元，尽管布拉德并没有那么多钱。这一裁决允许他们变卖他的个人财产，并将所得款项交给海莉。在没有塔米陪伴的情况下长大对海莉来说极其艰难，但她拒绝让这场悲剧定义自己。

66
01:01:29.000 --> 01:02:08.000
After graduating high school, she studied criminal justice at university before getting married and having a son of her own. The unconditional love her mother gave her has been an ongoing motivator for Hailey, who continues to look up to Tammy and aspire to be the type of parent she was. Looking back, Hailey now realizes that just because her father wasn't physically violent, it doesn't mean he wasn't abusing Tammy in other ways. Brad was known to constantly hover over Tammy, often not letting her out of his sight.
高中毕业后，她在大学学习了刑事司法，随后结婚并生下了自己的儿子。母亲给予她的无条件爱一直是海莉不断前行的动力，她始终敬仰塔米，并渴望成为像她那样优秀的父母。回首往事，海莉现在意识到，仅仅因为她的父亲没有进行身体上的暴力，并不意味着他没有以其他方式虐待塔米。众所周知，布拉德经常在塔米身边阴魂不散，常常不让她离开自己的视线范围。

